 },
 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.267,
   "text": "Today: Why Do We Have Seasons?"
  },
  {
   "start": 2.567,
   "end": 5.842,
   "text": "Here's what we'll cover. First: The Tilted Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.992,
   "end": 8.077,
   "text": "Second: Going Around the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.227,
   "end": 10.227,
   "text": "Third: Summer and Winter."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.377,
   "end": 12.772,
   "text": "And finally: Spring and Autumn."
  },
  {
   "start": 13.072,
   "end": 15.175,
   "text": "Part 1: The Tilted Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.325,
   "end": 19.415,
   "text": "Have you ever wondered why it is hot in summer and cold in winter?"
  },
  {
   "start": 19.415,
   "end": 24.09,
   "text": "Many people think the Earth gets closer to the Sun in summer. That is not true."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.09,
   "end": 26.817,
   "text": "The real reason is that the Earth is tilted."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.067,
   "end": 31.036,
   "text": "Our planet spins on an axis that leans about twenty-three degrees,"
  },
  {
   "start": 31.036,
   "end": 33.642,
   "text": "like a spinning top that is slightly crooked."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.042,
   "end": 37.952,
   "text": "Key takeaway: The real reason is that the Earth is tilted."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.502,
   "end": 40.781,
   "text": "Part 2: Going Around the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.931,
   "end": 45.15,
   "text": "The Earth also travels around the Sun. One trip takes one year,"
  },
  {
   "start": 45.15,
   "end": 49.325,
   "text": "or about three hundred and sixty-five days. Because of the tilt,"
  },
  {
   "start": 49.325,
   "end": 55.016,
   "text": "the same part of the Earth leans toward the Sun for part of the trip and leans away for another part."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.416,
   "end": 59.047,
   "text": "Key takeaway: The Earth also travels around the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 59.597,
   "end": 61.802,
   "text": "Part 3: Summer and Winter."
  },
  {
   "start": 61.952,
   "end": 64.396,
   "text": "When your half of the Earth leans toward the Sun,"
  },
  {
   "start": 64.396,
   "end": 68.176,
   "text": "sunlight hits the ground more directly. The days are longer,"
  },
  {
   "start": 68.176,
   "end": 72.201,
   "text": "and the land warms up. That is summer. When your half leans away,"
  },
  {
   "start": 72.201,
   "end": 76.741,
   "text": "the sunlight comes in at a low angle and spreads out. The days are shorter,"
  },
  {
   "start": 76.741,
   "end": 79.377,
   "text": "and it gets cold. That is winter."
  },
  {
   "start": 79.777,
   "end": 83.653,
   "text": "Key takeaway: The days are longer, and the land warms up."
  },
  {
   "start": 84.203,
   "end": 86.381,
   "text": "Part 4: Spring and Autumn."
  },
  {
   "start": 86.531,
   "end": 90.999,
   "text": "In between, the Earth is not leaning much toward or away from the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 90.999,
   "end": 94.749,
   "text": "Days and nights are about equal, and the weather is mild."
  },
  {
   "start": 94.749,
   "end": 98.799,
   "text": "These are spring and autumn. When it is summer in California,"
  },
  {
   "start": 98.799,
   "end": 103.863,
   "text": "it is winter in Australia, because the two places lean in opposite directions."
  },
  {
   "start": 104.263,
   "end": 109.803,
   "text": "Key takeaway: In between, the Earth is not leaning much toward or away from the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 110.353,
   "end": 115.443,
   "text": "So seasons come from the tilt of the Earth, not from how far away the Sun is."
  },
  {
   "start": 115.443,
   "end": 117.493,
   "text": "The next time you put on a warm coat,"
  },
  {
   "start": 117.493,
   "end": 120.068,
   "text": "remember that you are leaning away from the Sun,"
  },
  {
   "start": 120.068,
   "end": 122.966,
   "text": "and that the Earth is on its long trip around it."
  },
  {
   "start": 123.216,
   "end": 124.866,
   "text": "Thanks for watching!"
